    'story.skip': 'Skip the story, check now',
    'story.eyebrow': 'Free and private, for students applying abroad',
    'story.title': 'How study abroad scams trap students, step by step',
    'story.lead': 'Scammers use the same six steps again and again. Scroll to see each step and the free check that stops it.',
    'story.quickH': 'Or check something now:',
    'story.heroArt': 'Illustration: a letter, a phone, a stamp and a bank card floating around a green shield.',
    'story.scroll': 'Scroll to start the story',
    'story.railLabel': 'Story steps',
    'story.signLabel': 'The warning sign',
    'story.doLabel': 'Do this now',
    'story.checkLabel': 'The free check',
    'story.flip': 'Show the free check',
    'story.flipBack': 'Back to the warning sign',
    'story.s1.n': 'Step 1 of 6',
    'story.s1.title': 'A too-good offer',
    'story.s1.text': 'It starts with a message. An agent promises a place at a famous university and a full scholarship. It sounds like a dream.',
    'story.s1.sign': 'No one can promise admission or a visa. Only the university decides who gets in, and only the embassy decides the visa.',
    'story.s1.do': 'Do not reply or pay yet. Paste the message into the free check first.',
    'story.s1.check': 'Agent message check: paste a WhatsApp, SMS or email message. It looks for common scam patterns, like big promises and secrecy. The text never leaves your phone.',
    'story.s1.cta': 'Check a message',
    'story.s1.art': 'Illustration: a phone with a chat message full of big promises.',
    'story.s2.n': 'Step 2 of 6',
    'story.s2.title': 'A fake admission or scholarship letter',
    'story.s2.text': 'Next comes a letter. It has a logo, a stamp and a signature, so it looks real. But anyone can make a letter look real.',
    'story.s2.sign': 'Watch for a free email address like Gmail, spelling mistakes, a fee to pay within hours, or a request to keep it secret.',
    'story.s2.do': 'Log in to the university\'s own applicant portal yourself. Check that the same offer is shown there.',
    'story.s2.check': 'University check: see if the university is on an official register, like the UK student sponsor register or the Australian register for overseas students (CRICOS).',
    'story.s2.cta': 'Check a university',
    'story.s2.art': 'Illustration: an offer letter with a logo, a stamp and a signature.',
    'story.s3.n': 'Step 3 of 6',
    'story.s3.title': 'People pretending to be officials',
    'story.s3.text': 'Then someone calls. They say they are from the embassy, the university or the police. They know your name, and they sound official.',
    'story.s3.sign': 'Government offices do not phone you to demand money, and they do not threaten arrest to make you pay.',
    'story.s3.do': 'Hang up. Find the office\'s number on its own official website, and call back yourself.',
    'story.s3.check': 'Email or link check: paste the email address or link. It compares it with the university\'s real website and looks for lookalike tricks.',
    'story.s3.cta': 'Check an email or link',
    'story.s3.art': 'Illustration: a call from an unknown caller who says they are an official.',
    'story.s4.n': 'Step 4 of 6',
    'story.s4.title': 'Pressure to pay fast',
    'story.s4.text': 'Now the clock starts. "Pay today or you lose your seat." "The scholarship closes tonight." They want you to rush.',
    'story.s4.sign': 'Rushing is the scammer\'s best tool. Real deadlines are written on the university\'s own website.',
    'story.s4.do': 'Stop for one day. Show everything to a parent, a teacher or someone you trust.',
    'story.s4.check': 'Before you pay check: answer a few questions about the payment. It shows the warning signs before any money leaves.',
    'story.s4.cta': 'Check a payment',
    'story.s4.art': 'Illustration: a clock, an hourglass and a demand to pay at once.',
    'story.s5.n': 'Step 5 of 6',
    'story.s5.title': 'Payment to a personal account',
    'story.s5.text': 'They send bank details. The account is in a person\'s name, or it is a mobile wallet. They say it is faster this way.',
    'story.s5.sign': 'Universities take fees through their own portal, their own bank account or a payment service linked from their own website. Not through a person\'s account, a mobile wallet, cash or crypto.',
    'story.s5.do': 'Pay only through the official portal, or to the bank details on the university\'s own website.',
    'story.s5.check': 'Before you pay check: compare the account name with the university\'s name, and see the warning signs.',
    'story.s5.art': 'Illustration: a bank card, with money going to a person instead of a university.',
    'story.s6.n': 'Step 6 of 6',
    'story.s6.title': 'Threats and shame',
    'story.s6.text': 'When the student asks questions, the mood changes. There are threats, and "Do not tell anyone." Many students feel alone and ashamed.',
    'story.s6.label': 'Remember this',
    'story.s6.sign': 'Being scammed is never your fault. Scammers fool smart, careful people every day.',
    'story.s6.do': 'Tell someone you trust today. In danger right now? Call Rescue 1122 or Police 15.',
    'story.s6.flip': 'Show where to get help',
    'story.s6.helpLabel': 'Help you can get',
    'story.s6.check': 'Help: people and public services you can contact today, and what to do if you already paid. You do not have to face this alone.',
    'story.s6.cta': 'Open Help',
    'story.s6.art': 'Illustration: a phone with a threatening message, and a trusted person sending care.',
